From 0004000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K3 vs Raspberry Pi 5 Benchmark Project <benchmark-lab@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports: add a Linux Clang port for SpacemiT X100

LLVM now contains an upstream scheduling model for the SpacemiT X100 CPU.
Add an opt-in Linux port that selects this model, an explicit X100 ISA/ABI,
and scalar code generation.  The port inherits the POSIX timing and memory
implementation and does not change checksum-controlled workload sources.

The port is intentionally opt-in through PORT_DIR=linux-spacemit-x100.
Callers remain responsible for selecting a Clang build that supports
-mtune=spacemit-x100.
---
 linux-spacemit-x100/core_portme.mak | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 linux-spacemit-x100/core_portme.mak

diff --git a/linux-spacemit-x100/core_portme.mak b/linux-spacemit-x100/core_portme.mak
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..535b956
--- /dev/null
+++ b/linux-spacemit-x100/core_portme.mak
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
